(62061, 1677, 1005, '<td valign="top">Was it a bullseye?  I like this one.  I hope it wins.  What did it look like with a faster exposure?  I like the expression of motion, just curious if you <br/>tried to "stop" it.    Kewl darts.  Photo 10 Creativity 9 Games 10 total 10</td>', 'Was it a bullseye?  I like this one.  I hope it wins.  What did it look like with a faster exposure?  I like the expression of motion, just curious if you tried to "stop" it.    Kewl darts.  Photo 10 Creativity 9 Games 10 total 10', '2002-05-23 12:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62062, 1677, 811, '<td valign="top">Too cool and nice use of colors and motion trails.</td>', 'Too cool and nice use of colors and motion trails.', '2002-05-23 19:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62063, 1677, 1597, '<td valign="top">How did you get this shot, Nice</td>', 'How did you get this shot, Nice', '2002-05-23 22:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62064, 1677, 1226, '<td valign="top">Thats just... um.... just....<br/><br/>Wow!</td>', 'Thats just... um.... just....Wow!', '2002-05-23 23:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62065, 1677, 661, '<td valign="top">A game with action!</td>', 'A game with action!', '2002-05-24 23:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62066, 1677, 543, '<td valign="top">Did you use some kind of flash trigger, or is your timing just amazing?  Very impressive catch.  Love the specular motion blur from the fletching on the moving dart.  My only nits are the highlights on the two darts in the board and on the metal bits could use some smoothing out, and it looks like the focal point was just a bit forward of where it should be.  The DOF trails off right behind the bullseye.  I''m guessing the oversharp highlights are a result of trying to get sharpness out of a not-quite-in-focus foreground.  Top ten.</td>', 'Did you use some kind of flash trigger, or is your timing just amazing?  Very impressive catch.  Love the specular motion blur from the fletching on the moving dart.  My only nits are the highlights on the two darts in the board and on the metal bits could use some smoothing out, and it looks like the focal point was just a bit forward of where it should be.  The DOF trails off right behind the bullseye.  I''m guessing the oversharp highlights are a result of trying to get sharpness out of a not-quite-in-focus foreground.  Top ten.', '2002-05-25 02:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62067, 1677, 1822, '<td valign="top">Good photo. i would have liked it a little sharper</td>', 'Good photo. i would have liked it a little sharper', '2002-05-25 09:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62068, 1677, 280, '<td valign="top">OK, how long did it take you to get this just right? I think the bullseye could have been a little more to the right IMHO.</td>', 'OK, how long did it take you to get this just right? I think the bullseye could have been a little more to the right IMHO.', '2002-05-25 17:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(62069, 1677, 1169, '<td valign="top">great shot, a 10</td>', 'great shot, a 10', '2002-05-26 01:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
