(63015, 1743, 255, '<td valign="top">Very cool picture. Because this appeals to me, I have no criticism to offer! I wouldn''t even change the lighting because I like the shadow <br/>on the side of the dice. 10.</td>', 'Very cool picture. Because this appeals to me, I have no criticism to offer! I wouldn''t even change the lighting because I like the shadow on the side of the dice. 10.', '2002-05-24 13:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63016, 1743, 1202, '<td valign="top">This represents a lot of work with good results.</td>', 'This represents a lot of work with good results.', '2002-05-24 19:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63017, 1743, 689, '<td valign="top">Very nice  shot .... well lit and creative.</td>', 'Very nice  shot .... well lit and creative.', '2002-05-24 23:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63018, 1743, 244, '<td valign="top">One of my favorite shots. great idea and good execution, would have liked it better with 2 dice but just my opinion.</td>', 'One of my favorite shots. great idea and good execution, would have liked it better with 2 dice but just my opinion.', '2002-05-24 23:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63019, 1743, 543, '<td valign="top">Interesting effect.  Almost looks like you used two dice, or covered the lens during exposure (no trail from the lower moving die to the one in fg).  The blurry hand is a little distracting.  You might have held it very still, then dropped the die to bounce off instead of moving your hand to drop it.  Just an idea.</td>', 'Interesting effect.  Almost looks like you used two dice, or covered the lens during exposure (no trail from the lower moving die to the one in fg).  The blurry hand is a little distracting.  You might have held it very still, then dropped the die to bounce off instead of moving your hand to drop it.  Just an idea.', '2002-05-25 04:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63020, 1743, 1679, '<td valign="top">Very well thought. Excellent light and use of strobe.<br/>I think, however, that the hand could be a little more clear. It looks very fuzzy. I understand you wanted to show motion, but I think it needed something different.<br/>Maybe, you could have got away with a little less noise removal.<br/>Overall though, vert well thought and lit! Congrats!</td>', 'Very well thought. Excellent light and use of strobe.I think, however, that the hand could be a little more clear. It looks very fuzzy. I understand you wanted to show motion, but I think it needed something different.Maybe, you could have got away with a little less noise removal.Overall though, vert well thought and lit! Congrats!', '2002-05-25 08:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63021, 1743, 1128, '<td valign="top">Great movement</td>', 'Great movement', '2002-05-25 09:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63022, 1743, 441, '<td valign="top">nice shot, look forward to finding out how you did this!</td>', 'nice shot, look forward to finding out how you did this!', '2002-05-25 15:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63023, 1743, 428, '<td valign="top">Great shot! I love the way you have captured the movement of the dice, but getting the final one to be in such great focus! How many times did you have to try this?</td>', 'Great shot! I love the way you have captured the movement of the dice, but getting the final one to be in such great focus! How many times did you have to try this?', '2002-05-25 20:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63024, 1743, 1031, '<td valign="top">Nice multiple-exposure effect...</td>', 'Nice multiple-exposure effect...', '2002-05-26 01:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63025, 1743, 472, '<td valign="top">cool.  i wish the second die was also moving.</td>', 'cool.  i wish the second die was also moving.', '2002-05-27 12:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63026, 1743, 139, '<td valign="top">My favorite photo.  I can''t wait for the HOWTO on it.</td>', 'My favorite photo.  I can''t wait for the HOWTO on it.', '2002-05-27 00:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63027, 1743, 1528, '<td valign="top">nice long exposure<br/>too bad the hand couldn''t have been a little less blurry<br/>but i suppose that may have not been as realistic-looking, eh?</td>', 'nice long exposuretoo bad the hand couldn''t have been a little less blurrybut i suppose that may have not been as realistic-looking, eh?', '2002-05-27 00:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(63028, 1743, 1005, '<td valign="top">Connie, if you see this, I am really curious.  How did you pull this one off?  I am assuming a few tricks, like time exposure and maybe strobe, but try as I might to recreate this shot, I can''t.<br/><br/><br/>Please, please, please share your technique.  (I gave you a nine for this one!)  I know from the comments, I am not the only one.  How about in Tricks and Tips section?</td>', 'Connie, if you see this, I am really curious.  How did you pull this one off?  I am assuming a few tricks, like time exposure and maybe strobe, but try as I might to recreate this shot, I can''t.Please, please, please share your technique.  (I gave you a nine for this one!)  I know from the comments, I am not the only one.  How about in Tricks and Tips section?', '2002-05-29 17:47:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(63029, 1743, 326, '<td valign="top">Hi... Sorry I fogot to check this I was meaning to let you know. This shot was pretty simple. I used a piece of black construction paper, one side light, a tripod and 2 dice. The first dice is "still" in the picture. Then I worked on rolling the second dice behind the first one to give an effect of the second being the first. Hope that makes sense. I used 2 hands I was pressing the shutter while rolling the dice.</td>', 'Hi... Sorry I fogot to check this I was meaning to let you know. This shot was pretty simple. I used a piece of black construction paper, one side light, a tripod and 2 dice. The first dice is "still" in the picture. Then I worked on rolling the second dice behind the first one to give an effect of the second being the first. Hope that makes sense. I used 2 hands I was pressing the shutter while rolling the dice.', '2002-05-30 11:14:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(63030, 1744, 509, '<td valign="top">I really don''t like baseball, but this is nicely done</td>', 'I really don''t like baseball, but this is nicely done', '2002-05-20 01:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
